  "last_executor_claim": "Done. Deliverables in /app:\n\n- **cli_tool** — compiled C binary (zig cc, only libc dependency). Decodes the PNG via lodepng (28×28 grayscale), normalizes pixels /255, runs the 784→16→16→10 MLP parsed from `model.pth` (extracted via a torch-free unpickler since torch isn't installed), prints the argmax digit.\n- **weights.json** — all six tensors with shapes, matching the state_dict (input/hidden/output layer weights+biases).\n- **prediction.txt** — contains `2\\n`, matching the tool's stdout.\n\nVerified: `./cli_tool weights.json image.png` prints `2` and exits 0; both plausible MNIST preprocessings (raw /255 and standard mean/std normalization) independently agree on digit 2, so the prediction is robust to that choice.",
